			title: 'Your project’s ladder of offers',
			task: 'Build a ladder of five rungs and write a title and a text for each. 1) The lead magnet answers one narrow question of your audience; the form asks only for an email address and has two separate boxes (one for processing the data, with the word “processing” or “using”, and one for the newsletter, with the words “emails” or “news”), both unchecked in advance, and the button names what the person will get. 2) A low-priced first offer with the price as a number. 3) The core offer: the name of an item from the brief and a link with the main action from the brief in the same words. 4) An add-on and 5) a lighter option, both with a price named. The text has no pressure (“left”, “today only”, “hurry”). In the note, for each rung write the price (a number or “free”) and why the person needs it, and also where pressure could have appeared and what you replaced it with. For an expert, no guarantees or superlatives. Every “…” has to be replaced.',
