<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>{{title}}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section id="ladder-page">
        <h2>Offers</h2>

        <article class="rung" data-rung="lead">
          <h3>Free</h3>
          <p class="r-title">Checklist: what to prepare before your first call</p>
          <p class="r-text">A single sheet listing the documents and the questions; we need only an email address to send it.</p>
          <form class="lead-form">
            <p><label for="lm-email">Email</label><br><input id="lm-email" name="email" type="email"></p>
            <p><input id="lm-data" name="data" type="checkbox"> <label for="lm-data" class="consent-data">I agree to you using my email address to send me the checklist.</label></p>
            <p><input id="lm-news" name="news" type="checkbox"> <label for="lm-news" class="consent-news">I’d like to get emails with news. I can unsubscribe with one click in any email.</label></p>
            <button type="submit">Get the checklist</button>
          </form>
        </article>

        <article class="rung" data-rung="tripwire">
          <h3>A low-priced first offer</h3>
          <p class="r-title">A review of your documents</p>
          <p class="r-text">A short meeting after which you know what to do next. The price is $40, named in advance, and there is no renewal.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="rung" data-rung="core">
          <h3>The core offer</h3>
          <p class="r-title">{{items.0.title}}</p>
          <p class="r-text">The work from the first step to the result: the order of work, the time and the price are named before it starts.</p>
          <p><a class="cta" href="#contacts">{{mainAction.label}}</a></p>
        </article>

        <article class="rung" data-rung="upsell">
          <h3>An add-on</h3>
          <p class="r-title">Support after the result</p>
          <p class="r-text">You can add it to the main work or order it later at the same price: $20. A separate choice, not checked in advance.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="rung" data-rung="downsell">
          <h3>A lighter option</h3>
          <p class="r-title">A consultation without a visit</p>
          <p class="r-text">If you don’t need the full scope right now: a written review of your documents, $30.</p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>

    <aside class="note" data-scaffold id="ladder-notes">
      <h2>The ladder: prices and why each rung</h2>
      <table id="ladder">
        <tr><th>Rung</th><th>Price</th><th>Why the person needs it</th></tr>
        <tr class="row">
          <td>Free</td>
          <td class="price">free</td>
          <td class="why">To understand the order of work, giving nothing but an email address</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="row">
          <td>Low-priced first offer</td>
          <td class="price">$40</td>
          <td class="why">To check whether the project suits them, at little risk</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="row">
          <td>Core</td>
          <td class="price">from $200</td>
          <td class="why">To solve the whole job</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="row">
          <td>Add-on</td>
          <td class="price">$20</td>
          <td class="why">To consolidate the result, if they need it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="row">
          <td>Lighter option</td>
          <td class="price">$30</td>
          <td class="why">To get part of the benefit, if they need less right now</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p>Where on the ladder pressure could have appeared, and what I replaced it with: <span id="pressure-notes">Only real deadlines are named, the add-on is not checked in advance, the price and terms are visible at once, and the newsletter has a separate box.</span></p>
    </aside>
  </body>
</html>
`
